  "contract": [
    "Use original GetElementBoundingScreenRect only at event or popup polling boundaries: it flushes layout. Revalidate control identity after it returns.",
    "Original ConvertTo handles cross-document transforms, visual viewport resolution, ancestor transforms/scroll and desktop widget origin. Its result uses top-level chrome CSS units.",
    "nsPIDOMWindowOuter is a secondary base; its original Itanium offset-to-top identifies the complete outer window before WindowUtils.",
    "DOMRect stores the four output doubles at byte 48; guarded original allocation initializes that span. Release through original DOMRect::Release.",
    "Transport the full projected screen rectangle independently of the untransformed native model and raster viewport. GNUstep uses original NSAffineTransform in backing-window global coordinate conversions.",
    "Chrome CSS density is quantized to app units and can differ from the platform desktop scale. Convert all four screen rectangle coordinates by the original AppUnitsPerDevPixelInTopLevelChromePage and GetDesktopToDeviceScale values; never assume devicePixelRatio equals output scale.",
    "The independent browser oracle uses original toScreenRect device-pixel bounds divided by original window.desktopToDeviceScale. The initial918 report only checked CSS-unit transport agreement, so it cannot establish desktop-unit alignment. Preserve919 failure and the175% visual drift separately."
  ],
  "guards": "pinned-geometry.h:guard_projected_geometry_calls"
}
